.TH "RBACKUP" "1" "2026-08-16" "rbackup 0.3.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rbackup \- simple encrypted backup manager written in Elvish and built
on top of rclone
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]rbackup\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] \f[B]generate\f[R]
[\f[I]PATH\f[R]\&...
| \f[B]\-\f[R]] \f[B]rbackup\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] \f[B]gc\f[R]
\f[B]rbackup\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] \f[B]fetch\f[R] \f[B]rbackup\f[R]
[\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] \f[B]delete\f[R] \f[B]rbackup\f[R]
[\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] \f[B]version\f[R] \f[B]rbackup\f[R] \f[B]\-h\f[R] |
\f[B]\(enhelp\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]rbackup\f[R] is an Elvish script that compresses, encrypts,
uploads, and restores backup archives using \f[CR]rclone\f[R],
\f[CR]openssl\f[R], and \f[CR]zip\f[R].
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
\f[B]generate\f[R] [\f[I]PATH\f[R]\&... | \f[B]\-\f[R]]
Compacts specified paths into a ZIP file (or reads paths line\-by\-line
from standard input when \f[B]\-\f[R] is specified), encrypts it using
\f[CR]openssl\f[R] with \f[CR]RBACKUP_ENCRYPT_PASSWORD\f[R], and uploads
the archive to the configured \f[CR]rclone\f[R] remote location.
.TP
\f[B]gc\f[R]
Purges garbage\-collected backup archives from the \f[CR]rclone\f[R]
remote, keeping only the specified number of recent backups.
.TP
\f[B]fetch\f[R]
Downloads the encrypted backup at the specified index (defaults to
\f[CR]0\f[R] for the most recent backup) from the \f[CR]rclone\f[R]
remote, decrypts it, and extracts the contents into a temporary
directory.
.TP
\f[B]delete\f[R]
Deletes the encrypted backup at the specified index (defaults to
\f[CR]0\f[R] for the most recent backup) from the \f[CR]rclone\f[R]
remote.
.TP
\f[B]version\f[R]
Display the version of the application.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\-r, \(enremote \f[I]REMOTE:FOLDER/PATH\f[R]
Specify the destination \f[CR]rclone\f[R] remote and target directory.
Overrides the \f[CR]RBACKUP_RCLONE_REMOTE\f[R] environment variable.
.TP
\-k, \(enkeep \f[I]NUM\f[R]
Specify the number of backup archives to retain when running the
\f[CR]gc\f[R] subcommand.
Defaults to \f[CR]1\f[R] (or \f[CR]RBACKUP_KEEP_COUNT\f[R]).
.TP
\-p, \(enprefix \f[I]PREFIX\f[R]
Specify a custom prefix for the backup file name.
Defaults to \f[CR]backup\f[R] (or \f[CR]RBACKUP_FILE_PREFIX\f[R]).
.TP
\-i, \(enindex \f[I]INDEX\f[R]
Specify the index of the backup file to fetch or delete.
Defaults to \f[CR]0\f[R] (the most recent backup archive).
.TP
\-d, \(endry\-run
Perform a dry run for the \f[CR]gc\f[R] subcommand, listing files that
would be purged without deleting them.
.TP
\-j, \(enjunk\-paths
Do not save directory names in the backup archive.
Only the file names are stored.
Useful for flattening the backup structure.
.TP
\-h, \(enhelp
Display usage and help information.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
RBACKUP_RCLONE_REMOTE
Default \f[CR]rclone\f[R] remote destination in
\f[CR]REMOTE:FOLDER/PATH\f[R] format.
.TP
RBACKUP_ENCRYPT_PASSWORD
Password used for OpenSSL archive encryption and decryption.
Must be set prior to running \f[B]generate\f[R] or \f[B]fetch\f[R].
.TP
RBACKUP_FILE_PREFIX
Default prefix for the backup file name.
.TP
RBACKUP_PATHS
Colon\-separated (\f[CR]:\f[R]) list of default file system paths to
include in the backup.
.TP
RBACKUP_KEEP_COUNT
Default number of backup archives to keep during garbage collection.
.TP
RBACKUP_JUNK_PATHS
Set to \f[CR]1\f[R] or \f[CR]true\f[R] to enable flattening of paths by
default (equivalent to \f[CR]\-j\f[R] / \f[CR]\-\-junk\-paths\f[R]).
.SH EXAMPLES
\f[B]Create an encrypted backup of specified directories:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
export RBACKUP_ENCRYPT_PASSWORD=\(dqsecret\-passphrase\(dq
rbackup \-\-remote myremote:backups/myhost generate /home/user/documents /home/user/pictures
.EE
.PP
\f[B]Create an encrypted backup by streaming paths from standard
input:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
export RBACKUP_ENCRYPT_PASSWORD=\(dqsecret\-passphrase\(dq
find /home/user/documents \-type f \f[B]|\f[R] rbackup \-\-remote myremote:backups/myhost generate \-
.EE
.PP
\f[B]Clean up old backups, retaining the 5 most recent archives:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
rbackup \-\-remote myremote:backups/myhost \-\-keep 5 gc
.EE
.PP
\f[B]Fetch and decrypt the most recent backup:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
rbackup \-\-remote myremote:backups/myhost fetch
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[CR]rclone(1)\f[R], \f[CR]openssl(1)\f[R], \f[CR]zip(1)\f[R]
